 
<section xml:id="exercises">
  <title>Exercises</title> 
<exercise>
        <introduction>
          <p>Consider the following system of linear equations in variables <m>x_{1}, x_{2}, y_{1}, y_{2}, y_{3}, y_{4}</m>:</p>
          <me>\begin{aligned}
            x_{1} + y_{1} &amp;= 1,\\
            -x_{1} + y_{2} &amp;= 0,\\
            x_{2} + y_{3} &amp;= 1,\\
            -x_{2} + y_{4} &amp;= 0
          \end{aligned}</me>
        </introduction>
        <task>
          <statement><p>Write down the augmented matrix.</p></statement>
        </task>
        <task>
          <statement><p>Put the augmented matrix in reduced row echelon form</p></statement>
        </task>
        <task>
          <statement><p>What is the dimension of the solution set?</p></statement>
        </task>
        <task>
          <statement><p>Give an explicit parametrization of the solution set.</p></statement>
        </task>
      </exercise>

      <exercise>
        <introduction>
          <p>Consider the following matrix:</p>
          <me>\begin{pmatrix}
            0 &amp; 0 &amp; 1 &amp; 3 \\
            0 &amp; 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 0 \\
            0 &amp; 1 &amp; 0 &amp; 2 \\
            1 &amp; 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 1
          \end{pmatrix}</me>
        </introduction>
        <task>
          <statement><p>Put the matrix in reduced row echelon form.</p></statement>
        </task>
        <task>
          <statement><p>Suppose this is the augmented matrix of a linear system. Will that linear system be consistent? Explain why or why not.</p></statement>
        </task>
      </exercise>

      <exercise>
        <statement>
          <p>Consider the following matrix:</p>
          <me>\begin{pmatrix}
            0 &amp; 0 &amp; 1 &amp; 3 \\
            0 &amp; 1 &amp; 0 &amp; 2 \\
            0 &amp; 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 0
          \end{pmatrix}</me>
          <p>Suppose this is the coefficient matrix of a linear system. For which right hand sides is it consistent?</p>
        </statement>
      </exercise>
</section>
